# Use case 2 — the decomposition is a judgment, so something has to check it.

@meta
use_case: Contract renewals arriving with changed terms, about 40 a quarter
author: Team 2
date: 2026-09-21
approver: J. Lindqvist, Commercial Counsel
exit_criterion: Shut down if a material change is missed more than 1 time in any 12 months

@assumptions
- The signed version of every contract is retrievable and is the correct comparison baseline
- Clause section identifiers are stable between the signed version and the renewal
- Counterparties send renewals as text, not as scanned images

@unit
definition: One renewal, with its changed clauses grouped by the obligation they affect
kind: judgment
two_people_test: Two counsel would argue about where one obligation ends and the next begins
checked_by: A deterministic crosscheck confirms every changed clause appears in exactly one unit; any clause in none is listed for a human
fanout: 4
fanout_reason: Bounded by counsel review capacity, and renewals of one counterparty are judged together

@steps
1 | fetch | mechanical | code | Pull renewals due within 60 days and diff each against the signed version | batch
2 | group | mechanical | code | Group changed clauses by section identifier into candidate units | batch
3 | select | coordination | code | Order by contract value and renewal date, capped at the budget | batch
4 | gate-scope | gate | code | Refuse high-value or restricted counterparties before any clause is assessed
5 | assess | thinking | model | Decide whether a changed clause is cosmetic, material, or a new obligation
6 | crosscheck | test | code | Confirm every changed clause appears in exactly one unit and none was dropped
7 | gate-coverage | gate | code | Refuse when a clause belongs to no unit or to more than one
8 | prove | mechanical | code | Write the diff, the grouping, the coverage result and the assessment, then checksum it
9 | deliver | coordination | code | Write a review pack assigned to the named approver

@gates
4 | contract value is over 250000 USD, or the counterparty is on the restricted list | Route to counsel before any clause is assessed, with the full diff attached
7 | a changed clause appears in no unit, or in more than one | Return the clause list to the contracts owner and have a person reconcile it before review
9 | proof checksum differs from the checksum recorded when it was written | Stop the review pack and have the contracts owner establish who edited the proof and when

@evidence
writer_step: 8
artifact: The clause diff, the grouping into units, the coverage crosscheck, and the assessment of each change
integrity: SHA-256 recorded at write time and re-checked before the pack is sent

@record
transitions: memory/ledger.tsv, append-only, one line per transition, written by code only
units: memory/units.tsv, one row per contract with its outcome and the deciding step
retention: the contract term plus 2 years
acceptance: memory/acceptances.tsv, SHA-256 chained, carrying the design digest and the signer

@kpis
cost per completed decision | cost | unmeasured
material changes missed | quality | 1 in the last 12 months
days from receipt to counsel review | throughput | 11 days
refusals per 100 renewals | control | not applicable before this loop
renewals countersigned before the notice deadline | tvr-velocity | unmeasured
